          </zone-style>
        </zone>
        <zone flipboard-zone-id='5' h='42427' id='6' story-point-id='1' type-v2='text' w='96850' x='787' y='16494'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>Q2 What are Actions in Tableau? Explain how Filter Action can help hospital management analyze patient data.</run>
            <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>Answer:- </run>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='12'>Actions in Tableau are interactive features that allow users to trigger changes in visualizations based on user interaction such as clicking or hovering. A Filter Action enables one chart to filter data in other charts dynamically. In a hospital dashboard, this helps management analyze patient data efficiently—for example, selecting a department can instantly show its patient count, treatment cost, and outcomes. This improves decision-making by allowing focused and real-time data exploration.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
      </zones>
      <simple-id uuid='{2BD20E98-29E3-4211-B378-CFD3C4CBC692}' />
    </dashboard>
